index 0000000..4d7a5f9
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/architecture/public-part-receipts.md
@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+# Public Part receipts
+
+The public `knowledge.parts.Part` accepts positive integer or nonempty opaque
+string versions. The boundary definitions do not restrict Part versions to
+integers. Values are preserved without coercion; opaque versions are identities,
+not sortable chronology. Private `parts.Part` and its integer revision ordering
+remain a separate generation/authoring model.
+
+Snapshot ingestion retains public Parts, including draft and retired definitions,
+and typed source-document records needed to resolve their citations. This is a
+hash-join guarantee: the existing SourceDoc parser drops unknown extensions
+(such as `also_filed_as`), so receipts are not archival copies of raw documents. Each judged
+`PublishedSpec` also carries its Part version and the original Provenance,
+separately from Planning's `admitted_by`. Receipt values are deep copies so
+editing a result cannot mutate the input snapshot.
+
+This closes snapshot ingestion for the Emblem content-derived Part versions.
+It does not activate draft Parts or convert nominal dimensions to fitted widths.
+Admitted specifications still emit `published_spec_unapplied`: mapping public
+definitions and their exact dimensions into generation remains separate work.
+
+Validated by `tests/knowledge/test_public_part_receipts.py`. The actual Emblem
+snapshot is additionally exercised from fence-rag's
+`scripts/validate_emblem_public_parts.py`; the verification checks its original
+snapshot hash and exact Part round trips, not a rewritten fixture identity.
